@startuml
' ============================================================================
'  CodeReviewAgent - the full review flow, both platforms (feature 007)
'
'  Swimlanes: Developer, GitHub/TFS, Workflow, Agent, LLM.
'  Both platform branches, story-source selection, chunk planning, per-chunk
'  calls with their two kinds of retry, the synthesis pass, degraded paths,
'  deduplication and DRY_RUN.
'
'  The notes carry a worked example. Its numbers are ILLUSTRATIVE - issue #7,
'  PR #12, four files, two chunks - chosen to show every branch once, not taken
'  from a recorded run. A real default-budget review of four files is one call.
'
'  Render with:
'    java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg docs/review-flow.puml
'  SVG, not PNG: the PNG writer truncates tall diagrams at 4096px without
'  warning unless -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=8192 is passed.
'  Graphviz is not required (modern activity syntax).
'
'  Owners of each stage are named in [brackets]; docs/code-structure.md has
'  every file. The local-mode, TFS-only view is docs/local-mode-pr-review-activity.puml.
' ============================================================================

title AI code review - full flow (TFS and GitHub)\n<size:11>PLATFORM=tfs|github  -  STORY_SOURCE=tfs|github-issues|none  -  DRY_RUN defaults to true</size>

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam NoteFontSize 10
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1

|Developer|
start
:Open or push to a pull request;
note right
  **Example**: issue #7 "Add item to cart"
  with 3 acceptance criteria.
  PR #12 says "Closes #7" and changes 4 files:
  Interfaces.cs, CartService.cs,
  CartController.cs, Cart.cs
end note

|GitHub/TFS|
if (Platform?) then (GitHub)
  :pull_request event: opened, synchronize,
  reopened or ready_for_review;
  |Workflow|
  if (Draft PR, or head repo is a fork?) then (yes)
    :job **skipped** prints the reason;
    note right
      Never pull_request_target:
      fork code never sees secrets.
    end note
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  :concurrency group per PR:
  a newer commit **cancels** the older run;
  :check out the agent at agent_ref,
  pip install, then
  ""python -m review_agent --local""
  with GITHUB_TOKEN (permissions:
  contents read, PRs + issues write);
else (TFS)
  :branch-policy build, or a manual run
  (""TFS_API_VERSION=5.0"" on this server);
  |Agent|
  :bootstrap: fetch the agent repository
  and re-run inside it, unless --local
  [bootstrap.py, source_fetch.py];
endif

|Agent|
:load_config: PLATFORM picks the settings
that are required; every problem at once
[config.py];
if (Configuration valid?) then (no)
  :print every problem;
  :exit **2** (setup failure);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:make_platform: TfsPlatform over TfsClient,
or GitHubClient (a posting client is built
**only** when DRY_RUN=false)
[platform.py, github_client.py];

|GitHub/TFS|
:read the pull request;
|Agent|
switch (STORY_SOURCE)
case (tfs)
  |GitHub/TFS|
  :linked work items;
case (github-issues)
  |GitHub/TFS|
  :GraphQL closingIssuesReferences
  + "Closes #N" in the body,
  deduplicated, this repo only;
  :read each issue;
  |Agent|
  :criteria from "## Acceptance criteria"
  [stories.py, models.py];
  note right
    **Example**: #7 yields criteria 1-3,
    keyed wi7:c1 .. wi7:c3
  end note
case (none)
  |Agent|
  :checklist-only review, said so;
endswitch
|Agent|
if (Story readable?) then (no: 403)
  :story half lost, **stated**;
  note right: the review continues
else (yes)
endif

:checklist corpus: clone the checklist repo,
read every .xlsx / .docx into citable rules
[checklist.py, checklist_docs.py];

|GitHub/TFS|
:revision: TFS iteration, or GitHub head
and **merge base** (compare API);
:changed files (every page) and blobs;
|Agent|
:unified diffs; exclusions and bounds,
each skipped file with its reason
[diff_builder.py, selection.py];
|GitHub/TFS|
:read the agent's prior comments
(ai-review: markers);
|Agent|

if (Anything reviewable?) then (no)
  :summary "nothing to review";
else (yes)
  :plan chunks by **token budget**
  (LLM_MAX_PROMPT_TOKENS, default 120,000),
  group related files; cut oversized files
  on hunks, each piece with a skeleton
  [chunk_planner.py, declarations.py];
  note right
    **Example**: budget lowered so the
    planner makes **2 chunks**:
    1: Interfaces.cs + CartService.cs
    2: CartController.cs + Cart.cs
    The outline in BOTH lists
    removed  AddItem(int, int)
    added    AddItem(int, int, string)
  end note
  :build one prompt per chunk:
  rules, contract, story, scope, checklist,
  **PR outline**, the chunk's diff
  [prompt_builder.py];

  repeat :next chunk;
    |LLM|
    :review the chunk;
    |Agent|
    if (HTTP 429 / 5xx / timeout?) then (yes)
      :transport retry (up to 3 sends),
      each send logged with its tokens
      [llm_adapter.py, llm_log.py];
    else (no)
    endif
    if (Response matches the contract?) then (no)
      :one stricter retry;
      if (Still no?) then (yes)
        :degraded summary posted;
        :exit **0** - an outage
        never gates a merge;
        stop
      else (no)
      endif
    else (yes)
    endif
  repeat while (More chunks?) is (yes)
  ->no;

  :merge chunk findings and change notes
  [parser.py];
  if (More than one chunk?) then (yes)
    |LLM|
    :**synthesis**: outline + merged findings
    + notes + criteria -> one summary,
    final verdicts, cross_file_issues;
    |Agent|
    if (Synthesis usable?) then (yes)
      :apply verdicts and cross-file issues;
    else (no)
      :keep the chunk findings,
      **note** "synthesis did not complete";
    endif
    note right
      **Example**: chunk 2 saw
      CartController still calling
      AddItem(productId, quantity).
      Synthesis reports ONE cross-file
      issue naming Interfaces.cs and
      CartController.cs
    end note
  else (no)
  endif
  :build the report; usage line:
  tokens and estimated cost
  [parser.py, llm_log.py];
endif

:route findings: anchored to a changed line
-> inline; otherwise -> summary only.
Drop any whose marker was already posted
[output_layer.py, dedupe.py];
note right
  **Example**: 1 cross-file issue (inline
  on CartController.cs), 1 checklist
  violation (inline), criteria table:
  1 appears addressed, 2 not addressed
  (neutral, no comment), 3 possible
  contradiction
end note

if (DRY_RUN?) then (true - the default)
  :print exactly what would be posted;
else (false)
  |GitHub/TFS|
  if (Platform?) then (GitHub)
    :summary: one issue comment,
    edited in place on re-runs;
    :ONE review (event COMMENT) with
    every inline comment;
    if (HTTP 422: an anchor refused?) then (yes)
      :re-post the review listing each
      finding and its location instead;
    else (no)
    endif
  else (TFS)
    :summary thread (PATCH in place,
    or append); one thread per inline;
  endif
endif

|Workflow|
if (llm_log input?) then (true)
  :upload the log as an artifact,
  3-day retention (contains source code);
else (false)
endif

|Agent|
if (FAIL_ON_CONTRADICTION and blocking findings?) then (yes)
  :exit **1**;
else (no)
  :exit **0**;
endif
note right
  **Example re-run**: same commit ->
  suppressed=2 inline=0,
  summary edited in place
end note
stop

legend bottom
  Exit codes: 0 reviewed or degraded | 1 blocking findings (FAIL_ON_CONTRADICTION only) | 2 setup failure
  Worked-example numbers are illustrative. Detail: docs/code-structure.md, docs/github-setup.md
endlegend
@enduml
